[gd_scene load_steps=11 format=3 uid="uid://captvccb3v043"]

; The HOST's unit — ADR-0217 dec. 3, built by #744. A Godot INHERITED SCENE whose base is
; `addons/exmateria_sprite_rig/UnitRig.tscn`, and the sprite rig's ONE declared mount in
; `check_lattice_scene.py`.
;
; 🔴 WHY THIS FILE CHANGED SHAPE. Before #744 the rig lived in `src/animation/` and this
; scene named four of its files directly by `ext_resource` — the shader plus
; `SpriteLayerManager`, `AnimationStateController` and `CameraRelativeRenderer`. The move
; turned all four into a host file naming an ADDON path, which criterion 4 arm 1 scores.
; They are now ONE `PackedScene` line. 114 files reference this scene (5 production, 109
; `tests/`) and not one of them changed: every node path off the root is byte-identical,
; which is the whole reason this is inheritance rather than a wrapper node (ADR-0204
; dec. 2's argument, applied a third time after the camera and the cursor).
;
; 🔴 CHILD ORDER IS PRESERVED WITH `index=`, NOT BY LUCK. Inheritance appends the base's
; children first, so the seven host nodes below each carry the index they held before the
; split. `UnitMesh` is index 0 in the base; `SpriteLayerManager`,
; `AnimationStateController` and `CameraRelativeRenderer` come from the base and keep
; positions 6, 7 and 8. Nothing addresses a unit child by index today, but three of these
; scripts have a `_ready`, and `_ready` order IS child order.
;
; 🔴 THE UNIT MATERIAL IS NOT AUTHORED ANYWHERE IN THIS TREE ANY MORE, and it never
; mattered: `Unit.gd::_initialize_materials()` replaces it with
; `UnitAssets.base_material().duplicate()` — i.e. `assets/materials/unit.tres` — and calls
; `surface_set_material(0, …)`. The base scene keeps a texture-free `ShaderMaterial` so the
; editor preview is an untextured quad instead of a white one; the three
; `res://assets/sprites/textures/*.tga` lines this file used to carry are gone rather than
; moved, because moving them into the addon is exactly the P4 regression #741 and #744
; just paid for.

